nightsaver is an OLED-friendly Xorg and Wayland screensaver and PAM
screen locker written in Rust. It is a drop-in replacement for the
xscreensaver daemon and the xscreensaver-command control client: it
accepts xscreensaver's daemon flags, speaks its control protocol, and
reads the relevant subset of ~/.xscreensaver.

Every frame passes through an OLED guard that caps brightness, slowly
shifts pixels and periodically rests on a fully black screen. It ships
built-in clock, starfield, matrix and blank patterns, manages DPMS and
covers multiple monitors. Screen locking authenticates through OpenPAM
using unix-selfauth-helper, so nightsaver itself is not setuid.

Wayland support is experimental. On wlroots compositors such as sway
and labwc it blanks through layer-shell and locks with
ext-session-lock-v1; on KWin it can blank but not lock. GNOME Wayland
is not supported.
